.Dd 2026-11-07
.Dt LBTS-REINDEX 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts reindex
.Nd rebuild the index from the stored messages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts reindex
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command rebuilds the index of a LightBTS instance from the messages stored in
.Pa .lightbts/messages .
All information about tickets is contained in these messages,
the index only allows LightBTS to find it quickly.
.Pp
Messages are indexed in the order they were originally imported,
which is recorded in the X-LightBTS-Received header,
or with less precision in the Received header that LightBTS adds.
For messages that have neither, the Date header is used.
A reply is always indexed after the message it replies to.
.Pp
Tickets keep the numbers they have in the current index:
a message that creates a ticket gets the number of the ticket it belonged to, if that number is still free.
If no message creates a ticket anymore,
for example because its first message is gone, or it now belongs to another ticket,
the ticket no longer exists, and its number will not be reused.
If there is no index, tickets are numbered in the order they were created.
.Pp
The index is rebuilt in a single transaction:
if anything goes wrong, the current index stays as it is.
No hooks are run.
.Pp
If the index is damaged, or has a version that this version of LightBTS does not support,
remove the file
.Pa .lightbts/index
and run this command to create a new one.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The command exits with status 1 if any message file could not be indexed,
for example because it is not a valid message,
or because it is not stored under the name that its Message-ID determines.
The other messages are still indexed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 ,
.Xr lbts-import 1 .
